# The lint plugin interface. A rule is a meta object: a name, a stable code, a note, and a spot that inspects one AST node and tells a finding. Rules are ordinary Seed, authored in .tree and loaded by the lint engine, so a new rule is a new file, never an edit to the engine. The node is the type-checked AST node as a dynamic value (read its fields by name: node/form, node/op, node/left, node/span). tell reports a finding at a span. See note/library/seed/lint-plugins.md.

form rule
  link name, like text
  link code, like text
  link note, like text
  link spot
    like task
      take node, like dynamic
      take tell
        like task
          take message, like text
          take span, like dynamic
